hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2813","Narrated to us 'Isa bin Ibrahim Al-Ghafiqi, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that Salim informed him from his father (Abdullah bin Umar), who said: \Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) would lead the people of Makkah in prayer"," offering two Rak'ahs"," then he would give the Tasleem (conclude the prayer)"," and then they would stand up and complete their prayer.\"" Salim further said: When Al-H"""
